- If both factors are negative and large in absolute value
- Mixed signs will give negative products

For $(a-b)(c-d)$ to be maximum:
- Case 1: Both factors positive and large: $a > b$ and $c > d$, maximize $(a-b) \times (c-d)$
- Case 2: Both factors negative: $a < b$ and $c < d$, then $(a-b)(c-d) = (\text{negative})(\text{negative}) = \text{positive}$

